          customActions: [],
          deckDescription: 'One 24-card German-suited deck for Dreeg (Nürnberger Dreck): four suits (Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells) with six ranks per suit (9, 10, Unter, Ober, King, Ace). Used across the eight phases of the game; no jokers. The same deck is used for 66-style and Wenz/Solo phases in Franconian play.',
          suitDescription: 'Four German suits: Acorns (Eichel), Leaves (Laub), Hearts (Herz), Bells (Schellen), each with six cards. Trump is determined by turned card or by bid depending on the phase. Follow suit when able; ranking and point values follow 66 and Schafkopf conventions as used in Dreeg.',
          rankDescription: 'Six ranks per suit from low to high: 9, 10, Unter, Ober, King, Ace. Point values: Ace 11, Ten 10, King 4, Ober 3, Unter 2, Nine 0. The same ranking applies across Dreeg phases (66, Wenz, Solo, etc.) with phase-specific trump and lead rules.',
