          hero: {
            title: 'Dreeg (NÃ¼rnberger Dreck)',
            subtitle: 'Trick-taking rules and play flow',
            tagline: "Dreeg (a Franconian dialect form of 'Dreck', meaning trash or muck) is a complex, multiphase card game from the Nuremberg region of Germany.",
          },
          shortDescription: "Dreeg (a Franconian dialect form of 'Dreck', meaning trash or muck) is a complex, multiphase card game from the Nuremberg region of Germany. It is a composite game consisting of eight distinct sub-games, all based on the mechanics of Sechsundsechzig (66). Players compete to erase 'strokes' from their slate, and the game is strictly one of elimination: in each phase, players drop out as they succeed, until only one 'loser' remains to face the next challenge.",
